    {
      "id": "g06-04",
      "title": "Give or ask permission with てもいいです",
      "sourcePages": "152",
      "meaning": "Say an action is allowed, or ask whether it is allowed.",
      "formation": "Verb te-form + もいいです; add か for a permission question.",
      "notes": [
        "Permission concerns whether an action is acceptable, not whether the speaker has the ability to do it.",
        "A short positive reply can be いいですよ or どうぞ. てもいい cannot stand alone without its verb.",
        "も may be dropped in conversational speech, but the model keeps it."
      ],
      "prerequisites": [
        "g06-01"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "english": "May I use the computer?",
          "japanese": "パソコンを使ってもいいですか。",
          "kana": "ぱそこんをつかってもいいですか。"
        }
      ],
